+## Beginning-of-request uncertainty
+
+After bounded inspection, record low/medium/high uncertainty and its concrete cause, separately from difficulty. Clear outcomes/checks/resource bounds support low; unresolved dependencies or interpretations raise it. The label is not a calibrated probability. Ask the user when the remaining uncertainty changes a consequential choice about scope, cost, reversibility or acceptance; present the smallest useful options and a recommendation. Inspect retrievable facts first and continue independent authorized groundwork. Reuse existing decisions, including the shared change-request allowance; workers, retries and follow-ups do not repeat the question or refill it. Unknown usage remains unknown.
 
