 ## Earlier basis retained
 
-The six v5 sources were assessed from abstracts on 17 September 2026. Their transfer is the skill's inference; thresholds remain manual defaults.
+V5's six sources were assessed from abstracts on17September2026: [Loop-Back Authority](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14767) motivates evidence classes/drift/ladder; [Difficulty-Aware Topology](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13890) motivates recorded difficulty/light routing; [LIMBO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14138) motivates retrieval budgeting; [Interactive Memory Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.17088) motivates downstream utility records; [Recoverability](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13672) motivates evidence-bound resume decisions; [PipeSwift](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.16491) motivates completion-time/dependency accounting only. Reporting, verified coding, conversational memory and serving results do not establish this skill's thresholds or benefits. Self-reports/utility attribution remain uncalibrated/confounded; no trained router or learned allocator is installed.
 
-- **[Loop-Back Authority](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14767)**: a paired reporting experiment motivates evidence classes, drift checks and the judgment ladder; one task and model judges do not establish an optimal stopping threshold.
-- **[Difficulty-Aware Topology Selection](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13890)**: verifier-backed coding motivates recording difficulty and the lightest useful topology. This skill uses a self-report, not the paper's trained router.
-- **[LIMBO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.14138)**: memory competes with reasoning/verification for resources. Motivates the retrieval allowance and cost ledger, not its learned policy or demonstrated savings here.
-- **[Interactive Memory Learning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.17088)**: delayed conversational feedback motivates downstream utility records. Manual attribution remains confounded, not causal proof.
-- **[Recoverability](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.13672)**: restoration and later completion can conceal an invalid starting point. Motivates resume validation, current authority and version amendments, without host enforcement.
-- **[PipeSwift](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.16491)**: completion-oriented serving motivates dependency-aware dispatch and timing only; serving gains do not transfer to this workflow.
-
-V4, 12 September 2026, adapted these sources:
-
-- **[ExecCritic](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.09133v1)**: independently qualify behavioral tests and protect them from repair-driven weakening. Failure on the original alone does not prove the expectation correct.
-- **[Long-running harnesses](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents)** and **[application harness design](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/harness-design-long-running-apps)**: progress artifacts, recovery and separate evaluation; engineering reports, not universal comparisons.
-- **[MAPLE](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.11636)**: retain actual programs, plans and candidates; no optimizer is required.
-- **[Grounding Agent Memory](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11060v1)**: scoped environment probes before admission; domain-specific results and curation costs limit transfer.
-- **[Fortunate Recall](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10413v1)** and **[What Should an Agent Forget?](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10263v1)**: lifecycle validity and stored/current/history views; neither qualifies concurrent coding memory.
-- **[Studying Without a Syllabus](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10824v1)**: bounded preparation; extra context can mislead.
-- **[ORCH](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11737v1)**: coordination follows dependencies; prepared simulations do not establish online hierarchy evolution.
-- **[RobustSGPO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.09646)**: scoped between-run patches, retained snapshots and rollback, without importing search schedules or scores.
+V4's12September2026 sources: [ExecCritic](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.09133v1) for independently qualified/protected behavioral tests; [long-running harnesses](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents) and [application harnesses](https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/harness-design-long-running-apps) for progress/recovery/evaluation; [MAPLE](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.11636) for actual retained artifacts; [Grounding Agent Memory](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11060v1) for scoped environment probes; [Fortunate Recall](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10413v1) and [What Should an Agent Forget?](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10263v1) for lifecycle/current/history separation; [Studying Without a Syllabus](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.10824v1) for bounded preparation; [ORCH](https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11737v1) for dependency-aware coordination; [RobustSGPO](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.09646) for scoped between-run patches/rollback. These domain-specific papers/reports do not qualify concurrent coding memory, universal orchestration or online evolution here. A test failing on an original artifact alone does not validate its expectation. More preparation/curation can cost resources and mislead. Original detailed assessments remain archived.
 
